---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const comparisons = [
  ['Senior expertise advises', 'Senior expertise builds'],
  ['Requirements cross teams', 'One operator connects design and execution'],
  ['Capacity grows with staffing', 'AI extends the senior builder’s reach'],
  ['Implementation ends at handoff', 'Build, run and keep improving'],
];

const artifactMarkup = `<div class="material-object" aria-hidden="true">
  <img src="/finance-material.png" width="1672" height="941" alt="" decoding="async" />
  <svg class="material-trace" viewBox="0 0 1672 941" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"><path class="material-base" fill="none" stroke="#c1dbff" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="11 10"/><path class="material-plan" fill="none" stroke="#ffac70" stroke-width="5"/><circle class="material-result" r="11" fill="#ffc089" stroke="#ffd5aa" stroke-width="3"/></svg>
  <div class="record-callout record-one"><span>01 / CASH TODAY</span><strong data-record-value="cash">$1,200,000</strong></div>
  <div class="record-callout record-two"><span>02 / MONTHLY BURN</span><strong data-record-value="burn">$75,000</strong></div>
  <div class="record-callout record-three"><span>03 / PLANNED HIRES</span><strong data-record-value="hiring">2 × $10,000</strong></div>
</div>`;
---
<Layout title="Thriai — Don't hire a consultant. Hire a builder.">
  <div class="opening" id="opening">
    <div class="system-track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="system-stage">
      <div class="system-atmosphere"></div><div class="material-hero" data-material-slot="opening"><Fragment set:html={artifactMarkup} /></div>
      <div class="system-fallback"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
      <canvas id="system-canvas"></canvas>
      <div class="scene-index"><span class="scene-dot"></span> <span id="scene-label">01 / CONNECT THE INFORMATION</span></div>
    </div></div>
    <section class="builder-hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Senior finance expertise.<br class="mobile-only" /> Hands-on AI implementation.</p>
      <h1 id="hero-heading"><span>Don't hire</span><span>a consultant.</span><span class="builder-line">Hire a builder<span class="orange-period">.</span></span></h1>
      <div class="mobile-material-slot" data-material-anchor="hero" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="hero-bottom"><p>Thriai designs, builds and runs your AI-native finance function. The senior expert who understands your business is the person implementing the systems—and stays involved in operating them.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#demo">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Talk about your business <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
      <div class="hero-footnote"><span>JUDGMENT → SYSTEMS → DECISIONS</span><span>SCROLL TO CONNECT <b aria-hidden="true">↓</b></span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="delivery-section wrap" aria-labelledby="delivery-heading">
      <span class="record-disclosure">SYNTHETIC INPUTS / ILLUSTRATIVE MODEL</span>
      <div class="section-number">01 / THE DELIVERY MODEL</div>
      <div class="delivery-heading"><h2 id="delivery-heading">A different<br />delivery model.</h2><p>The person who sees how it should work<br />is the person who builds it.</p></div>
      <div class="comparison-table" role="table" aria-label="Comparison of delivery models">
        <div class="comparison-row comparison-head" role="row"><span role="columnheader">A traditional consulting model</span><span role="columnheader">The Thriai approach <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span></div>
        {comparisons.map(([before,after],i)=><div class="comparison-row" role="row"><span role="cell"><small>0{i+1}</small>{before}</span><span role="cell">{after}</span></div>)}
      </div>
      <p class="comparison-note">A comparison of operating models; individual firms and engagements vary.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="reach-section wrap" aria-labelledby="reach-heading">
      <div class="section-number">02 / WHY IT WORKS</div>
      <h2 id="reach-heading">AI changes<br />what a senior<br />expert can <em>deliver.</em></h2>
      <div class="mobile-material-slot" data-material-anchor="model" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="reach-copy"><p>Experienced operators know how the pieces should fit together. AI gives a hands-on expert greater reach to build the connections.</p><p>Integrations. Automated workflows. Financial models. Information connected across the business. Senior judgment stays close to the work, from the first architectural decision through everyday operation.</p><p class="reach-statement">The expertise stays human.<br />The capacity keeps expanding.</p></div>
    </section>
    <div class="light-transition" aria-hidden="true"><span>INFORMATION BECOMES A DECISION.</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="light-world">
    <section class="proof-section wrap" aria-labelledby="proof-heading">
      <div class="section-number">03 / FROM OPERATING EXPERIENCE TO WORKING SYSTEMS</div>
      <div class="proof-intro"><h2 id="proof-heading">Built inside<br /><span>a real finance</span><br />function.</h2><div><p class="large-copy">The business judgment<br />and the ability to build it.</p><p>Thriai grew out of Eric Anderson’s hands-on work connecting finance, planning, revenue operations and AI at a mid-market SaaS company.</p><p>Eric combines that implementation experience with finance leadership, acquisition support and investor reporting. The person designing your finance function understands the decisions it needs to support.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about">Meet your builder <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="proof-disclosure">Founder operating experience, separate from Thriai client engagements.</p></div></div>
      <div class="decision-demo" id="demo">
        <div class="demo-heading"><div><span class="demo-badge"><i aria-hidden="true"></i> ILLUSTRATIVE WORKING DEMO</span><h3>Can we afford<br />the next hires?</h3></div><p>One question. Connected cash and hiring assumptions. Change an input and follow the decision through.</p></div>
        <noscript><p class="notice">The scenario below is shown at its default assumptions. Enable JavaScript to adjust the inputs and recalculate.</p></noscript>
        <div class="demo-workspace"><span class="model-signal" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="demo-controls"><form class="demo-inputs" id="scenario-form" aria-label="Illustrative hiring scenario">
            <div class="demo-step">01 / THE INPUTS</div>
            <label for="cash">Cash today <span>USD</span><div class="input-shell"><b>$</b><input id="cash" name="cash" type="number" min="1" max="100000000" step="1" value="1200000" aria-describedby="demo-error" required /></div></label>
            <label for="burn">Monthly net cash burn <span>BEFORE HIRES</span><div class="input-shell"><b>$</b><input id="burn" name="burn" type="number" min="1" max="10000000" step="1" value="75000" aria-describedby="demo-error" required /></div></label>
            <label for="hires">Planned hires <output for="hires" id="hire-count">2 people</output><input id="hires" name="hires" type="range" min="0" max="6" step="1" value="2" /></label>
            <label for="hire-cost">Monthly cost per hire <span>FULLY LOADED</span><div class="input-shell"><b>$</b><input id="hire-cost" name="hireCost" type="number" min="1" max="100000" step="1" value="10000" aria-describedby="demo-error" required /></div></label>
            <p class="demo-error" id="demo-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
          </form>
        <details class="demo-assumptions"><summary>See the arithmetic and assumptions <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p id="formula">$1,200,000 ÷ ($75,000 + 2 × $10,000) = 12.6 months.</p><p>Synthetic inputs, not client data or a client result. Hires start immediately. Burn and employee costs stay constant; no revenue growth, financing, severance, hiring fees or interest. The chart covers 12 months and stops at zero. A real decision also needs timing, revenue scenarios and an agreed minimum cash buffer. This is an arithmetic demonstration, not an AI-generated recommendation.</p></div></details>
          <div class="demo-process-note" data-demo-beat="model"><span>02 / THE CONNECTION</span><h4>The hiring record joins the cash model.</h4><p>The added monthly cost flows into the same cash forecast. The solid line shows the change; the dashed line keeps the original plan in view.</p></div>
          <div class="demo-process-note" data-demo-beat="decision"><span>03 / THE DECISION</span><h4>Carry the tradeoff forward.</h4><p>The same record and graph become a brief. Senior judgment still needs to weigh start dates, revenue scenarios and the cash buffer.</p></div></div>
          <div class="working-journey"><div class="working-stage"><div class="demo-result" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
            <div class="working-record" data-working-record><span class="record-id">H–01 <i aria-hidden="true"></i></span><span class="working-record-label">PLANNED HIRES / SYNTHETIC</span><strong data-working-value="hiring">2 × $10,000</strong><span class="working-record-total"><b data-working-value="additional">$20,000</b> / month added</span></div>
            <div class="working-sheet"><div class="record-socket" aria-hidden="true">H–01 / HIRING ASSUMPTION</div><span class="sheet-spine" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="sheet-title"><span class="sheet-model-title">CASH MODEL</span><span class="sheet-decision-title"><span class="decision-long">DECISION </span>BRIEF / H–01</span></div>
            <div class="runway-number"><strong data-baseline-value="runway" hidden>16.0</strong><strong id="runway">12.6</strong><span data-runway-context>months of runway<br />with the planned hires</span></div>
            <svg class="cash-chart" viewBox="0 0 540 180" role="img" aria-labelledby="chart-title"><title id="chart-title">Illustrative cash balance: current plan versus planned hires over 12 months.</title><defs><clipPath id="working-area-reveal"><rect data-working-reveal x="20" y="0" width="500" height="180" /></clipPath><linearGradient id="chart-fill" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#3761ff" stop-opacity=".17"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#3761ff" stop-opacity="0"/></linearGradient></defs><path d="M20 24H520M20 80H520M20 138H520" stroke="#d9dfe6" fill="none"/><path clip-path="url(#working-area-reveal)" id="cash-area" d="M20 24L520 132L520 138H20Z" fill="url(#chart-fill)"/><path id="baseline-line" d="M20 24L520 109.5" stroke="#9ea7b5" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/><path pathLength="1" id="hiring-line" d="M20 24L520 132.3" stroke="#244df5" stroke-width="3"/><circle id="cash-endpoint" cx="520" cy="132.3" r="5" fill="#ff834a"/><text x="20" y="167">TODAY</text><text x="520" y="167">MONTH 12</text></svg>
            <div class="chart-legend"><span><i class="legend-base"></i> Before hires</span><span><i class="legend-hire"></i> With hires</span></div>
            <div class="working-cash"><span>Cash at month 12</span><strong data-baseline-value="remaining" hidden>$300,000</strong><strong data-working-value="remaining">$60,000</strong></div>
            <div class="demo-answer"><div class="demo-step" data-answer-context>THE TRADEOFF / SYNTHETIC SCENARIO</div><p data-working-explanation hidden>Current burn only. H–01 has not yet been applied to this forecast.</p><p id="decision-answer">Two hires add $20,000 to monthly burn and reduce runway by 3.4 months. At month 12, the model leaves $60,000 in cash.</p><button class="working-skip" type="button" data-working-skip>Show hiring result <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><div class="working-progress" aria-hidden="true"><span>01 RECORD</span><i></i><span>02 MODEL</span><i></i><span>03 BRIEF</span></div></div>
          </div><div class="working-action-distance" aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
    <section class="benefits-scene" data-working-benefits aria-labelledby="benefits-heading" data-finance-scene="benefits">
      <div class="section-number">04 / WHAT IT MAKES POSSIBLE</div>
      <h2 id="benefits-heading">Build the foundation once. <span>Keep expanding</span> what it can do.</h2>
      <div class="benefit-triptych"><article><span>01 / THE BUDGET</span><h3>Preserve<br />runway.</h3><p>Automate recurring work, consolidate overlapping tools and reduce dependence on disconnected service providers. Put more of your budget toward building the business.</p></article><article><span>02 / THE DECISION</span><h3>Get answers while<br />decisions are still open.</h3><p>Bring financial and operating information together. Explore performance, cash and hiring with AI grounded in your company’s data, supported by an experienced finance operator.</p></article><article><span>03 / THE NEXT STAGE</span><h3>Be ready when the<br />questions get harder.</h3><p>Give your board, investors and external reviewers consistent reporting and a clear path to the underlying records. Carry that foundation into fundraising, diligence and your next stage.</p></article></div>
    </section>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="finance-story story-visual" id="working-story">
    <section class="scope-scene" id="services" aria-labelledby="scope-heading" data-finance-scene="scope"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-number">05 / A CONNECTED FINANCE FUNCTION</div>
      <div class="scope-scene-heading"><h2 id="scope-heading">Each part makes<br />the others<br /><em>more useful.</em></h2><p>The information that runs your books should inform your forecast, support a board discussion and help answer an investor’s question. We bring bookkeeping, cash operations, planning, reporting and systems into one operating approach.</p></div>
      <div class="finance-folio" aria-label="Explore the three connected practices">
        <a href="/pricing" class="folio-plane folio-revenue"><span class="folio-label">01 / THE CONNECTIONS <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span><h3>Revenue<br />Systems</h3><p>Revenue operations and financial data that work together.</p><div class="folio-etch etch-records" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span class="folio-bottom">Connected records</span></a>
        <a href="/pricing" class="folio-plane folio-platform"><span class="folio-label">02 / THE FOUNDATION <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span><h3>AI Finance<br />Platform</h3><p>Connected information, automated workflows and useful AI access.</p><div class="folio-etch etch-model" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span class="folio-bottom">Working systems</span></a>
        <a href="/pricing" class="folio-plane folio-cfo"><span class="folio-label">03 / THE JUDGMENT <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span><h3>Fractional<br />CFO</h3><p>Financial leadership, planning and an ongoing operating relationship.</p><div class="folio-etch etch-decision" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div><span class="folio-bottom">Better-informed decisions</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="scope-scene-footer"><span>ONE OPERATING APPROACH. AN ENTIRE FINANCE FUNCTION.</span><a class="text-link" href="/pricing">Explore scopes and published pricing <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="engagement-scene wrap" aria-labelledby="engagement-heading" data-finance-scene="engagement">
      <div class="section-number">06 / AN ONGOING RELATIONSHIP</div>
      <h2 id="engagement-heading">Build. Run.<br /><span>Keep improving.</span></h2>
      <div class="open-brief">
        <div class="brief-page"><span class="brief-record-stamp" aria-hidden="true">H–01</span><span class="brief-kicker"><i class="scene-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i> ILLUSTRATIVE DECISION BRIEF</span><h3>The model informs.<br />Senior judgment<br />stays involved.</h3><p class="brief-decision" data-scenario="decision">Two hires add $20,000 to monthly burn and reduce runway by 3.4 months.</p><div class="brief-output"><span>Cash at month 12</span><strong data-scenario="remaining">$60,000</strong></div><svg class="brief-chart" viewBox="0 0 480 210" role="img" aria-label="The same illustrative cash model carried into the decision brief"><path d="M20 25H460M20 95H460M20 165H460" stroke="#b5c7e1" fill="none"/><path data-scenario-path="base" d="M20 25L460 130" stroke="#8a9bb4" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 5" fill="none"/><path data-scenario-path="plan" d="M20 25L460 158" stroke="#ec955c" stroke-width="3" fill="none"/><circle data-scenario-point="plan" cx="460" cy="158" r="5" fill="#ec955c"/><text x="20" y="197">TODAY</text><text x="460" y="197" text-anchor="end">MONTH 12</text></svg><div class="brief-question"><span>THE NEXT QUESTIONS</span><p>When should the hires start?<br />What if revenue changes?<br />What cash buffer do we need?</p></div><p class="brief-disclosure">Synthetic illustration, not a recommendation or client result. These questions sit beyond the simple arithmetic demo.</p></div>
        <div class="relationship-page"><p class="large-copy">A stronger foundation.<br />An operator who stays.</p><p>We understand the business, take ownership of the agreed finance responsibilities and build the systems that support them. Then we operate the function and keep improving it as your needs and AI capabilities evolve.</p><p>Whether you are establishing finance for the first time or giving an existing team a stronger foundation, the relationship starts with where you want the business to go.</p><div class="engagement-terms"><span>Defined scope</span><span>Published pricing</span><span>Your systems</span></div><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Talk about your business <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="closing-section"><div class="closing-beam" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="closing-artifact" aria-hidden="true"><i class="closing-records"><b></b><b></b><b></b><b></b></i><i class="closing-model"><b></b><b></b><b></b></i><i class="closing-decision"><b></b></i></div><div class="wrap"><span class="section-number">THE NEXT STAGE STARTS HERE</span><h2>Build the finance<br />function your<br /><span>next stage needs.</span></h2><div class="closing-bottom"><p>Tell us where the business is today<br />and what you want it to become.</p><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Talk about your business <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
  <script>import '../scripts/home';</script>
</Layout>

